---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **띠별로 스타의 이름.** (`/star-signs`)
 *
 * ⭐⭐ 사장님 지시(8/16·8/20) — 스타의 이름을 제목과 본문에. 손님은 이름을 검색한다.
 *
 * ── 🔴 이 지면이 절대 안 하는 것 ─────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ **점을 치지 않는다.** 우리는 이미 재서 발행했다 — 배우 1,047명의 띠 분포는
 *    카이제곱 7.77(문턱 19.68)로 **우연과 구분되지 않는다.** 첫 화면에 그 말을 둔다.
 * ⛔ **개별 풀이를 안 한다.** 사주 원국은 태어난 **시**가 필요하고 공개 프로필에 없다.
 * ⛔ **못 이은 사람을 0 으로 안 쓴다.** 이름은 싣고 수 자리를 비운다.
 * ⭐ 우리가 하는 것은 하나 — **누가 같은 띠인지 이름으로 보여 주는 것.**
 *
 * 🔴 Astro 앞말은 TypeScript 다. 🔴 JSX 는 끝 공백을 버린다 — {' '} 를 쓴다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import KcwCardnews from '../../components/KcwCardnews.astro';
import KcwShorts from '../../components/KcwShorts.astro';
import d from '../../data/wikitip-star-signs.json';

const 큰띠 = [...d.signs].sort((a, b) => (b.top[0]?.perMillion ?? 0) - (a.top[0]?.perMillion ?? 0));
const 으뜸 = 큰띠[0];

const TITLE = 'Which Korean stars share your Chinese zodiac sign? '
  + 'IU, Cha Eun-woo, Byeon Woo-seok and 1,044 more';
const DESC =
  `We placed ${d.peopleWithSign} Korean actors and singers into the twelve zodiac signs by year of `
  + `birth — IU and Song Hye-kyo in the Rooster, Cha Eun-woo and Song Joong-ki in the Ox, `
  + `Byeon Woo-seok in the Goat. The spread across signs is indistinguishable from chance, and we `
  + 'say so on the page.';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://www.wikidata.org/', 'https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}
  canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/star-signs">
  <h1>{TITLE}</h1>
  <p class="lead">{d.question}</p>
  <p class="q">
    {d.peopleWithSign} Korean actors and singers, sorted into the twelve signs by the year they
    were born. Within each sign the names are ordered by how often their own Wikipedia article is
    opened in Indonesia, Vietnam, Thailand and Malaysia — so the name you are most likely to know
    comes first.
  </p>

  {/*
    🔴 이 상자가 이 지면의 뼈대다. 이름을 늘어놓기 **전에** 못을 박는다.
      뒤에 두면 손님이 표부터 읽고 「이 띠가 좋구나」로 가져간다.
  */}
  <section class="warn-box">
    <h2>Read this first — this is not a prediction</h2>
    <p class="warn">{d.notAPrediction.says}</p>
    <p class="warn">{d.notAPrediction.whyNoReading}</p>
  </section>

  {d.signs.map((s) => (
    <section>
      <h2>{s.sign} — {s.people} Korean stars</h2>
      <p>
        {s.top.map((p) => p.name).join(', ')}
        {s.withReads > s.top.length ? ` and ${s.withReads - s.top.length} more we can measure` : ''}.
      </p>
      <div class="scroll-x">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Born</th><th>Reads per million</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {s.top.map((p) => (
              <tr>
                <td class="nm">{p.name}</td>
                <td class="fine">{p.born}</td>
                <td>{p.perMillion ?? '—'}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      {s.withoutReads > 0 && (
        <p class="note">
          Another {s.withoutReads} people in this sign have a date of birth but no read count we
          could match. They are counted in the {s.people}, and we leave their figure empty rather
          than writing zero.
        </p>
      )}
    </section>
  ))}

  <section>
    <h2>What this page cannot tell you</h2>
    {d.cannotSay.map((s) => <p class="note">{s}</p>)}
    <p class="note">{d.limitation}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>How this was counted</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Source</b> — {d.source}</li>
      <li><b>Window</b> — {d.window}</li>
      <li><b>Method</b> — {d.method}</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="note">
      <a href="/zodiac">The count that says the spread is chance</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/member-vs-group">Members and their groups</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/about">How we count</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <KcwCardnews set="signs" count={5} />

  <KcwShorts set="signs"
    says={`Fourteen seconds: the names in six of the twelve signs, and the measurement that says `
      + `the spread across signs is indistinguishable from chance.`} />

  {/*
    🔴 2026-08-22 — 이 지면은 띠를 다루면서 **방으로 가는 길이 0개**였다(실측).
      방 열두 장에 스타 이름 1,047개가 있는데 여기서 거기로 갈 수가 없었다.
      ⛔ 「만들어 놓고 문을 안 냈다」를 이 자리에서 다섯 번째로 겪는다. 길을 낸다.
  */}
  <section>
    <h2>The twelve rooms, with every name in them</h2>
    <p>
      The counting on this page is about the group. If you want the names, they are sorted into
      twelve rooms by birth year — <a href="/community">all twelve rooms are here</a> — and each
      room is named for the most-read Korean star born in that year: IU in the
      {' '}<a href="/room/rooster">Rooster room</a>, Bae Suzy in the
      {' '}<a href="/room/dog">Dog room</a>, Go Youn-jung in the
      {' '}<a href="/room/rat">Rat room</a>, Ma Dong-seok in the
      {' '}<a href="/room/pig">Pig room</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      <strong>A room name is not a reading.</strong> The rooms exist because a list of 1,047 names
      is not a page anyone finishes and twelve rooms of about ninety are. Sharing a year with IU
      means sharing a birth year and nothing else.
    </p>
  </section>


  {/*
    🔴 2026-08-22 — 새 지면 /day-pillar 를 냈는데 들어오는 문이 **기사 하나뿐**이었다(실측 2장).
      「만들고 문을 안 냈다」를 이 자리에서 여섯 번째로 겪지 않으려고 여기서 길을 낸다.
      ⛔ 이 지면과 저 지면은 «다른 축»이다 — 여기는 태어난 해(띠), 저기는 태어난 날(일주).
        같은 것을 두 번 세는 것이 아니라는 말을 문장으로 적는다.
  */}
  <section>
    <h2>The other axis — the day, not the year</h2>
    <p>
      This page sorts people by the year they were born. There is a second axis that almost
      nobody counts: the <a href="/day-pillar">day pillar</a>, the two characters for the day
      itself. We built it for 9,249 Korean entertainers — every English saju site reads one chart
      at a time, so nobody had a denominator until now.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      <strong>Two axes, not the same count twice.</strong> A birth year gives the zodiac sign on
      this page; a birth date gives the day pillar on that one. One of the four tests over there
      crossed the chance line, and we published everything we did to try to kill it rather than
      calling it a finding.
    </p>
  </section>
  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/star-signs" />
</WikiTip>

<style>
  .warn-box { border: 1px solid #b45309; border-radius: 6px; padding: 0.5rem 1rem; }
</style>
